# This repository contains no query results from any environment: no result row, no row count, and
# nothing inside one. A value a tenant emitted is named as an observed value where this pack
# publishes one at all, rather than reproduced as output.
#
# The rules below are the mechanical half of that. They exist because the accident this pack is
# most exposed to is not a decision to publish telemetry - it is `git add -A` after an export
# landed in the working directory. A pull-request diff lives under refs nobody can rewrite, so the
# cheap moment to stop that is before the commit.
#
# This is a backstop and not the control. The control is the Confidentiality section of README.md,
# the exclusion list in docs/scope-and-out-of-scope.md, and the attestation on every issue and pull
# request template. A file type that is not listed here is not thereby cleared to commit.

# Query and telemetry exports. These are the formats the Defender and Sentinel portals hand you
# when you export a result set.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.json
*.jsonl
*.ndjson
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.parquet

# Screenshots and captured images. The pack ships none and accepts none.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.webp

# Archives and compressed files, which hide any of the above inside them. The bare compression
# extensions are listed as well as the tar pairs, because *.tar.gz does not match an export
# compressed straight to results.csv.gz, and *.gz does.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz

# Portal logs and captured traffic. This is the likeliest single form of the accident the header
# above names.
*.log
*.har

# A gap this file has by design, stated rather than left to be discovered, and it is a property of
# the approach rather than a list. Any format that carries too much legitimate traffic in a
# documentation repository to exclude by default is unblocked here whatever it can also carry: *.txt
# is the plainest case, and *.md is the same case and a stronger one, being this pack's own format.
# The header applies: an unlisted type is not thereby cleared to commit.

# Scratch and working paths. Anything here is by definition not reviewed.
scratch/
tmp/
temp/
*.local
*.bak

# Agent and tooling state. This one is here because the rule that hides it today lives in the
# repository this pack is authored in, and that rule does not travel with the pack. A published
# copy would otherwise start with no rule for it at all.
.omc/

# Editor and OS artefacts.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
